{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions","id":24125,"title":"Some questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-05T19:28:27-08:00","id":24125,"title":"Some questions","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I am working on a character for a game and some questions came to my mind. <br /> <br /> 1) as my character will be a waterborn elemental, one of the things about elementals is their difficulty to interact with humanity and other changeling. I am wondering though how to just bring that accross that my character has difficulty now that she has come back from the hedge? <br /> <br /> 2.) How would religions interacting with changelings and the courts?<br /> <br /> -herkles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T23:36:38-08:00","id":24209,"title":"","content":"1) Mechanically that difficulty is represented by losing 10-agian on specific social rolls. This translates into your character not being incompetent in interactions, esp. if they've got some talent with it, but that they're detached enough that they have trouble in complex social situations (aka when you have people rolling vs. each other because their average successes are lower they'll lose such contests more often) and they rarely succeed by large margins. <br /> <br /> From a more role-playing perspective, there's a lot of ways of handling it which is an excellent place to add some quirks based on your character. Perhaps as a Waterborn your character tends to let words flow out without a lot of attention to syntax, pausing and other minor verbal cues, and frequently transitions to new topics in the same statement. All of this tends to make them hard to understand or follow in conversation, making people less likely to listen to them and making it harder for them to effectively communicate.<br /> <br /> 2) Lots, and lots of ways? There's no set response here. Every individual sit going to have their own reaction. The Courts, as a whole, are not presented as being terribly concerned with religion as a default. However Courts in a highly religious area might be impacted by this and different Courts might also trend towards gathering individuals of a similar reaction to religion after being taken to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:28:20-08:00","id":24599,"title":"","content":"Hello there~<br /> <br /> 1) I play an elemental, and the basic component of how I present that is to simply be dense and slow with social interaction, especially 'subtle(r)' ones. But beyond that, one of the more interesting and fun exercises is to re-imagine social behavior from the perspective of the element. How would water flirt, what emotions does it commonly feel, what are idioms and phrases it would use, how does it get what it wants or avoid being manipulated? It's a silly and fun project (or rather, an endearing but insane project - this is Changeling), and it can add a lot of quirks to your character.<br /> One of my favorite examples was a woodblood giving someone a queen honey-bee to express romantic interest. I don't have anything specific on hand for waterborn, but I'll share if they come up.<br /> <br /> Also, if available, <i>Winter Masques</i> gives more depth about the perspective and experiences of each Seeming.<br /> <br /> 2) There's no default reaction between changelings and religion, but any response is going to be to reconcile existing religious beliefs with what changelings experience. The themes and foundations of the game are rooted in psychological trauma, not in anything religious, so there's plenty of room for changelings and their Courts to adapt or adapt to religious beliefs as well.<br /> <br /> <i>Autumn Nightmares</i> had a lot of interesting explanations of the Keepers based on what the changelings experience - one such story was that the Fey are angels who didn't fight in the War, and were banished to a half-way realm for not supporting Heaven (a story rooted in one Catholic reconciliation with folk Irish myth, by the way). There are a lot of other aspects - the trials of Job, traitors in our midst, a war for the souls of mankind, various good and bad spirits in many religions, the half-human children of the Greek gods - where religious themes could parallel the lives of Changelings. I'd start with a good understanding of the religion(s) in mind and of the personal experiences of the changeling(s) to seek out good overlap. If their are commonalities across the freehold, that may be grounds for Court-wide foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T21:33:29-08:00","id":24892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=24209#post24209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Mechanically that difficulty is represented by losing 10-agian on specific social rolls. This translates into your character not being incompetent in interactions, esp. if they've got some talent with it, but that they're detached enough that they have trouble in complex social situations (aka when you have people rolling vs. each other because their average successes are lower they'll lose such contests more often) and they rarely succeed by large margins.<br /> <br /> From a more role-playing perspective, there's a lot of ways of handling it which is an excellent place to add some quirks based on your character. Perhaps as a Waterborn your character tends to let words flow out without a lot of attention to syntax, pausing and other minor verbal cues, and frequently transitions to new topics in the same statement. All of this tends to make them hard to understand or follow in conversation, making people less likely to listen to them and making it harder for them to effectively communicate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=24599#post24599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there~<br /> <br /> 1) I play an elemental, and the basic component of how I present that is to simply be dense and slow with social interaction, especially 'subtle(r)' ones. But beyond that, one of the more interesting and fun exercises is to re-imagine social behavior from the perspective of the element. How would water flirt, what emotions does it commonly feel, what are idioms and phrases it would use, how does it get what it wants or avoid being manipulated? It's a silly and fun project (or rather, an endearing but insane project - this is Changeling), and it can add a lot of quirks to your character.<br /> One of my favorite examples was a woodblood giving someone a queen honey-bee to express romantic interest. I don't have anything specific on hand for waterborn, but I'll share if they come up.<br /> <br /> Also, if available, <i>Winter Masques</i> gives more depth about the perspective and experiences of each Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I am looking for the perspectives of roleplaying this is out more. The advice you do provide does help out a bit. I like to try making my characters pop so to say, so getting this difficulty across is something I hope to be able to play up. The concept or at least the start of it anyways is the folktales of the Russian Rusalka; if this helps at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=24209#post24209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Lots, and lots of ways? There's no set response here. Every individual sit going to have their own reaction. The Courts, as a whole, are not presented as being terribly concerned with religion as a default. However Courts in a highly religious area might be impacted by this and different Courts might also trend towards gathering individuals of a similar reaction to religion after being taken to Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=24599#post24599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) There's no default reaction between changelings and religion, but any response is going to be to reconcile existing religious beliefs with what changelings experience. The themes and foundations of the game are rooted in psychological trauma, not in anything religious, so there's plenty of room for changelings and their Courts to adapt or adapt to religious beliefs as well.<br /> <br /> <i>Autumn Nightmares</i> had a lot of interesting explanations of the Keepers based on what the changelings experience - one such story was that the Fey are angels who didn't fight in the War, and were banished to a half-way realm for not supporting Heaven (a story rooted in one Catholic reconciliation with folk Irish myth, by the way). There are a lot of other aspects - the trials of Job, traitors in our midst, a war for the souls of mankind, various good and bad spirits in many religions, the half-human children of the Greek gods - where religious themes could parallel the lives of Changelings. I'd start with a good understanding of the religion(s) in mind and of the personal experiences of the changeling(s) to seek out good overlap. If their are commonalities across the freehold, that may be grounds for Court-wide foundations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T10:56:32-08:00","id":25880,"title":"","content":"*bump* <br /> <br /> I am still looking for ways of playing up the difficulties of interactions as a water elemental. <br /> <br /> also I am curious if there are/would be entitlements based around religions? we have similar things for the other creatures in WoD, so I am curious if their might be some for Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T14:04:27-08:00","id":26021,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of the Entitlements are built around specific religions. A few have strong religious themes and inspirations though. The Knighthood of the Dragonslayer are based around St. George in theme, but they're aren't a religious order. The Lost Pantheon believe that they are gods (or at least gods in the making) and seek to live out being deities to their own cults.<br /> <br /> But as far as I know, there's nothing more like an Entitlement of Christian changelings that seek to reconcile their natures with the Lord's plan or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T14:47:00-08:00","id":26058,"title":"","content":"An idea you might want to explore is a sect of changelings trying to revive a medieval form of Christianity. Medieval Christianity was full of people kludging the religion with local pagan myths, legends, and practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T20:18:41-08:00","id":26251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=26021#post26021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any of the Entitlements are built around specific religions. A few have strong religious themes and inspirations though. The Knighthood of the Dragonslayer are based around St. George in theme, but they're aren't a religious order. The Lost Pantheon believe that they are gods (or at least gods in the making) and seek to live out being deities to their own cults.<br /> <br /> But as far as I know, there's nothing more like an Entitlement of Christian changelings that seek to reconcile their natures with the Lord's plan or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah didn't know about them; but I might see what Entitlements I can come up with. I might post them on the forum if any are interested in, and of course to critique them and provide feedback for them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Randompaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=26058#post26058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea you might want to explore is a sect of changelings trying to revive a medieval form of Christianity. Medieval Christianity was full of people kludging the religion with local pagan myths, legends, and practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting idea, though also slightly tricky considering that their faith would be from what ever era they were taken. Though this is an avenue to look into.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question that came to my mind recently is about the other 'time' courts, dawn and dusk and sun and moon. How are politics done with them? as half a day, or less, seem like it would be difficult to do politics, even though I like courts philosophies. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T20:45:49-08:00","id":26265,"title":"","content":"In regards to religion entitlements, there is of course the Lost Pantheon, whereupon a changeling believes themselves to be divine, or close enough to it. While often they become atavistic icons or gods known from the age of myth, it's entirely possible one could believe themselves to be Jesus or Buddha or a figure from any number of modern religions. They even suggest the idea of urban legends such as Bloody Mary or the Jersey Devil. They can even &quot;distill Glamour out of the worship of mortals, though doing so necessitates the revelation of one's true form to the unensorcelled.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T10:06:38-08:00","id":26567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/24125-some-questions?p=26251#post26251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question that came to my mind recently is about the other 'time' courts, dawn and dusk and sun and moon. How are politics done with them? as half a day, or less, seem like it would be difficult to do politics, even though I like courts philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been ages since I read them (skimmed them? &gt;.&gt; ), so I can't remember if any advice or description was given in the write-up. Politics would still be in play, just different. There's an understanding that if you try to put forth a longer term policy, the other Court might shut that down and/or undo your work. There are a number of responses to this. To name the three that come easily to me:<br /> <br /> 1) A given Court does stuff the other won't find objectionable. If it's something nobody dislikes, the other Court <i>could</i> put forth effort to block you (and may do so for political reasons, depending), but incentives to do so aren't as obvious. There's likely some degree of staying out of each others' way.<br /> 2) A given Court persuades the other to permit/assist on a certain policy. This will usually involve non-trivial exchanges, whether of goods or knowledge or oath-sworn favors or whatever. Somewhat in line with 1), it may also mean simply permitting/assisting with a certain policy the other Court wants.<br /> 3) A given Court makes a sudden, dynamic declaration/action that gives the other Court little choice but to go along with it. If, say, one Court starts what amounts to a sudden war with another Freehold, supernatural group, etc. then the other Court may not be able to escape the consequences (e.g. victory might be possible if both Courts fight for it, but the freehold's toast or unacceptably diminished for sure if they don't). I imagine these are very significant instances, but undertaken very carefully because good <i>gog</i> will there be a ton of blowback and ill will for it.<br /> <br /> That's my reading on it, broadly speaking. Again, I could be way off in how they actually work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}